\f2\b0  Sexual transmission works, but it is 
\f1\b significantly less effective
\f2\b0  than a direct medical injection. Bodily fluids naturally carry a low viral titer. A sexual partner will catch it, but they only receive a trace, low-titer viral load that is quickly chewed up and silenced by their cell's methylation systems. It provides a weak, fleeting version of the panacea that cannot grant extended lifespan without a direct, high-volume medical injection.\
